  User-facing strings (T-111). English is the default locale and the fallback for every
  other: an untranslated key resolves here rather than rendering blank.

  No <plurals> anywhere, deliberately. T-123 moved every count out of its sentence
  ("Items needing attention: 3"), so no string has to agree with a number and no language
  needs a plural rule here - which is what makes Ukrainian (3 forms) and Arabic (6) cost
  nothing extra beyond translation.
-->
